 "increment": "tw-t1c",
 "previous": "tw-t1b",
 "phase": "T1c: gamepads on Android (the user's question 2026-10-11)",
 "change": "NTSDAndroid only: NTSDAndroidGamepads finds the first two input devices with SOURCE_GAMEPAD at launch (InputDevice.getDeviceIds/getDevice/getSources through JNI on the activity thread, every call exception-checked, local references deleted), keeps each one's axes (X/Y, HAT_X/HAT_Y) and A/B/X/Y (BUTTON_1-4 on generic pads) and d-pad keys from the input queue, and samples every 25 ms on the main queue with the SDL host's mapping (hat or d-pad keys over the stick, y down, buttons 1-4). Joystick motion and gamepad buttons from any device are consumed; d-pad keys and Back only from a gamepad found at launch. A cancelled motion and focus loss put the pads at rest. Before: 0 joysticks; stick motion reached the touch path as mouse moves near the top-left; B fell back to Back = Esc.",
 "review": "Independent review, round 1: defects - a cancelled joystick motion carries the last axes, so a direction could stick after focus loss or a disconnect (medium); generic pads' BUTTON_1-4 swallowed; a lone SOURCE_JOYSTICK node (a motion sensor) could take a slot; the d-pad/Back change to record. All fixed (cancel and focus loss reset, BUTTON_1-4 mapped, SOURCE_GAMEPAD required). Round 2: OK; a doc comment narrowed afterwards (comment only). Behaviour change recorded: a gamepad found at launch drives the joystick with its d-pad keys (as on macOS, SDL and the original) instead of arrow keys, and its Back no longer acts as Esc; system Back still does. Accepted gap: a button or stick held through a focus change reads as released until moved again.",
 "notes": "Scripted runs never probe or sample, so results cannot change. Gate on native eb4a848e (final 703f1f25 differs by a doc comment only): clean APK; emulator vs, joystick and demo equal, vs frames identical (1832); phone A/B with music and sounds: load 5.56-6.32 against 6.28-6.41 s, main 10.80-10.91 against 10.86 ms, render 7.13-7.15 against 7.51-7.55, process 27.07-27.22 against 27.25-27.62 - no regression. Emulator behaviour: with the previous APK an injected 'input gamepad keyevent KEYCODE_BUTTON_B' at the main menu ended the game (B -> Back -> Esc -> the quit question answered Yes; home screen shown); with the new APK the menu stays; system Back ('input keyevent KEYCODE_BACK') still ends it as before. The A12's own input devices (sources 0x80000101, 0x101, 0x1103, 0x301) are not gamepads, so it still reports 0 joysticks without a controller. Not checked: a real controller (needs one paired with the A12). Core, Runtime and Package.swift unchanged, so the other hosts' gates do not apply.",
